    By default, ``jnp.nanprod`` computes the product of elements along the flattened
    array.

    >>> nan = jnp.nan
    >>> x = jnp.array([[nan, 3, 4, nan],
    ...                [5, nan, 1, 3],
    ...                [2, 1, nan, 1]])
    >>> jnp.nanprod(x)
    Array(360., dtype=float32)

    If ``axis=1``, the product will be computed along axis 1.

    >>> jnp.nanprod(x, axis=1)
